Write a helper that returns spec-shaped data, then feed a sequence through `side_effect`:
```python
def simple_instance_list(status, pending):
    return {'DBInstances': [{'DBInstanceStatus': status,
            'PendingModifiedValues': pending, 'DBInstanceIdentifier': 'fakedb'}]}

rds_client_double = MagicMock()
rds_client_double.describe_db_instances.side_effect = [
    simple_instance_list('rebooting', {'a': 'b'}),
    simple_instance_list('available', {}),
]
```
This proves the module uses only parameters defined in the API spec.
